.TH VAULT-MIRROR 1 "September 2026" "vault" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vault-mirror \- mirror a website into an encrypted vault
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vault mirror
.RB [ \-\-key
.IR PATH ]
.RB [ \-\-vault
.IR DIR ]
.I URL
.RI [ FOLDER ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B vault mirror
crawls the website at
.I URL
and stores every page and asset it finds in the vault, beneath
.IR FOLDER / HOST
(or just
.I HOST
if no folder is given).
.PP
The crawl is single threaded: one request at a time, in breadth-first order.
It follows only links on the same host as
.IR URL ,
and requests are sent with a Chrome user agent string.
.PP
Links in HTML
.RB ( href ,
.BR src ,
.BR action
and
.B poster
attributes) and in CSS
.RB ( url(...) )
that point into the mirror are rewritten to relative paths, so the copy
browses correctly once fetched out of the vault. Links to other hosts, and
fragments, are left as they were.
.PP
Pages are named after their URL path. A path that is empty or ends in
.B /
becomes
.BR index.html ;
a query string is appended as
.BI _ query
(URL-escaped). Anything already stored under the same name is replaced.
.PP
A page that fails to download, or answers with anything but
.BR "200 OK" ,
is reported on standard error and skipped; the crawl carries on.
The vault is locked exclusively for the whole run.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-key " PATH"
Key file. Default: $VAULT_KEY, else ~/.vault/key.
.TP
.BI \-\-vault " DIR"
Vault directory. Default: $VAULT_DIR, else ~/.vault/store.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B VAULT_PASSPHRASE
Passphrase, instead of prompting on the terminal.
.SH EXAMPLES
Mirror a site into the vault under
.BR example.com/ :
.PP
.RS
vault mirror https://example.com/
.RE
.PP
Mirror it under a folder, then fetch the front page:
.PP
.RS
vault mirror https://example.com/ archive/2026
.br
vault get archive/2026/example.com/index.html
.RE
.SH LIMITATIONS
Links are found by pattern matching, not by parsing HTML: URLs assembled by
scripts, and
.B srcset
lists, are neither followed nor rewritten. There is no depth limit, rate
limit or robots.txt handling; only mirror sites you may copy.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vault (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Andy Dixon <vault@dixon.cx>, https://www.dixon.cx
